 the collection of samples, identification of bacterial isolates, handling of the database, multilocus sequencing analysis, pulsed field analysis, analysis of the data, and writing of the manuscript. AH participated in the establishment of the study, collection of the samples, the treatment of the patients, and writing of the manuscript. AAF was engaged in the collection of the samples, the treatment of the patients, and analysis of the data. VP participated in the collection of samples and isolation and characterisation of bacterial isolates. JPD was involved in the multilocus sequence analysis and pulsed field gel electrophoresis. TS contributed in the analysis of the demographic and epidemiological data and the spatial distribution of the meningitis cases and carriers of <named-content content-type="genus-species">N. meningitidis</named-content> in KND. MA was involved in the establishment of the study, pulsed field analysis, multilocus sequence analysis, and analysis of the data. SG participated in the establishment of the study, collection of samples, identification of bacterial isolates, multilocus sequence typing, analysis of the data, and writing of the manuscript. GP was responsible for the design and the supervision of the project and participated in the analysis of all data and writing of the manuscript. JL, AH, AAF, VP, JPD, TS, MA, SG, and GP critically revised the manuscript and gave their approval for submission of the final version.</p></fn><fn id="n101" fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding:</bold> The study was funded by the Stanley Thomas Johnson Foundation, the Meningitis Research Foundation, and the Meningitis Vaccine Project. The funders had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>